- If the tree is empty, return 0.
- Create a variable `sum`.
- Check if a left child exists.
- If the left child has no children, it is a left leaf; add its value to the sum.
- If it is not a leaf, recursively check its subtree.
- Also, check the right subtree, as it may also contain left leaves.
- Return the total sum.
Time Complexity: O(n)
In the worst case, we visit each node of the tree once. A constant number of checks is performed for each node.

Space Complexity: O(h) — due to the recursion stack.
 An iterative solution can be implemented using a stack or a queue. However, the time complexity will remain O(n).
